I personally dont like 'Oh... Sir' sequel. Yes, i agree that game became much deeper and pleasant in terms of possibilities and variabilities for building interesting insults, yet, it became less fun. First of all, there is more pause between words so it takes longer to talk (or atleast it looks like it). Second, 15 seconds is not enaught to read and understand all those sentences for someone who is not perfect god of english. I am seeing players doing a lot of mistakes, i do them as well, not because of missclicks, but cus we dont even understand which part of sentence this 'xxxx' should be put in. Right now there is no proper interface feature that can help you understand which words is usable there or there.
The next ptoblem is, most insults are way too much specific. It appears that a good part of those require some special treatment just like Hovercraft in prequel - its really hard to use it right. And there are way too many of such words. Moreover a good pile of people mentioned here are a mystery to me. We all know Gendalf, Harry Potter and Marilyn Monroe, but who the heck are these guys we insult in text? Well, just now i checked Steve Buscemi and do remember this guy from Boardwalk Empire, yet, 95% of others are unknown to me. I dont understand how to build sentences around them and it requres you much more then just knowing who they are. It feels like i am forced to actually be one of those celebrities to understand their world and therefor insult properly in game.
Now the last part, when you have first turn you get lots of possibilities, cus you probably just gonna steal the first 2 phrases good for damaging opponent. The second player often left with some crap which will deal 5-7 dmg in best scenario, but mostly will end up at 1-4. And, to be honest, all those mega smart insults are smart to an extent where they stop being funny and just become smart... Its not interesting to listen to them. I mean, in previous game there were lots of ways to harm opponent's pride, but right now it feels more like a bucket of vomit. I end up using 'your dog', 'next movie' and other things that i think are not an insults in a first place.
So, what can be done to improve game?
1) Add some more basic words and sentences, like mom and dad (i am missing those 'dumb and ugly', etc stuff);
2) Add 1 additional line of random words to the middle field, its now hard to build properly with increased vocabulary;
3) Songs with words inside which are played on background are not just ruining atmosphere of this game but also annoy a lot;
4) When game is minimized it should play sounds, which will help us understand when its time to get back to 'insults tab', since staring into monitor for 15 mins until i find opponent isnt right;
5) Some heroes are booring and anooying, like that bonsai girls and Monroe - if you gonna add more characters, make them agressive, loud and harsh like Serious Sam... So we can understand what they are saying;
6) Solo campaign (careere?) is kind-a booring, mostly cus enemies are mega dumb; and repeating the same quests for every hero is silly - give everyone different quests, so we have something interesting to aim for.

After completing both the original game,and the DLC's,here are my thoughs on the game,on a pro/con format.
PROS:
-Gameplay;
Let's start off with the most important aspect (at least in my opinion) of a game: the gameplay. Simply put, Arkane did a very good job in making the game as polished as it is. The movement is fantastic and it feels very smooth and fluid. Also, the addition of spells (especially blink) makes the world feel more dynamic and more fun overall .The stealth mechanics are good ,even though Dishonored is not a pure stealth game , the AI is ok and will give you quite some challenge (especially if you play without any of your powers).Also ,the Chaos mechanic adds an extra level of playability to the game, which is awesome and will give you multiple reasons to play it again.
-The world and level design;
The level design in Dishonored is great. Each level is complex, with multiple areas and side objectives in it. Also, the game gives you multiple choices as to how you want to finish the levels. For example, if have to enter a house, you can enter any way you want, be it thtough the roof (if you can), through the main door, or through the basement .I love the freedom there is in each level.
-The theme;
The world in Dishonored is placed in the city of Dunwall,a city infested with the Rat Plague .Thus ,you will find many abandoned buildings to explore,where you can find goods like runes or bone charms. Also, watch out for weepers when exploring.
-The sound and music;
The music is very well composed ,and fitting to the world. The sound effects are also great. The voice that whispers you stuff when casting a spells, as well as parrying a hit, makes for some overall great sound design.
-The graphics;
I left this point as the last here, because its probably the least important thing for me in a game. The art style is beautiful, the world is colourful and there is a perfect balance between stylized and realistic, which make the game pass the test of time pretty well.
CONS:
-Even though I said the AI can offer some challenge, overall the AI is a bit dumb.Sure, if  a guard finds a corpse, they will start searching, and even then, after a few seconds, they go back like "Nah,it's just rats." . It would have been cool if a guard would start searching for you just by seeing his mate missing. But that's just me, and many people have different opinions.
-The Quick Save isn't great;
-You can't have multiple "Quick Saves". When you press F5 for a Quick Save, it overwrites the previous one. If you accidentally save in a position where you can't escape, and you wanna finish the game as a ghost, there is no other option other than going to the Save menu, or restarting the entire mission alltogether.  This actually happened to me and it♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥me off.
THE VERDICT:
Overall, despite the cons I came up with, the huge pros of the game make them unsignificant. I would gladly play the game again ,and if you are a Stealth games fan, you OWE it to yourself to play this game, if you haven't allready.
With that said,I give Dishonored a 9.5/10!

