I played, finished and enjoyed H2S1, and I can understand that this is a different game. The big differences are camp creation, crafting changes and the multiplayer, but the comparisons in reviews are pretty ridiculous.
Here's what's negative that a few reviewers caught:
the user interface is really messy (ie. hard to find items in inventory, difficult to navigate crafting);
some movements and attacks can be sluggish at times (hitboxes and direction of attack feel off occasionally, zombies getting stuck in walls/doors/loops);
the world, while big, isn't open and can feel repetative and unfinished;
hit-or-miss, the chat is only macros written in the game and there's no messaging;
there are some loading/saving issues with online play, where a restart of the game is required and progress lost.
That said I feel that beyond the positives is trusting that the developers will work on these issues. These don't break the game, but they can be frustrating. The big question for recommending this game is whether or not they will invest more than just DLC.
In the end I think this game is really fun! Not just looking ahead at all the features and fixes it could have, right now:
the aiming system that H2S is unique and fun;
the environment is both pretty and creepy;
the characters and story are funny and engaging;
the zombies all feel different, and the combat doesn't seem repetative;
skills, leveling, the camp and crafting systems are combined in a very understandable and reasonable way;
and the multiplayer - while I'm just scratching the surface of it - is really well put together. I highly recommend partying up, because the chat system is pretty much non-existant.
I recommend this game as is, especially during its sale. I also feel that the developers and publishers are putting the necessary work in to the game to make it not just very functional, but even more fun than it already is.
I also received the Abandoned Backpage DLC for free after purchasing H2S1, but not as a package so I can't review it. All I have to say is that this DLC is not worth it - by the time you are leveled up enough to use the armour in the pack, it becomes obsolete and useless. Not recommended.

