A dating Sim with birds? Pah, that's ridiculous!... is what you are probably thinking. And you are right, but that is not the whole truth; beneath its satirical surface, Hatoful Boyfriend hides a gripping story that turns it into a very solid Visual Novel.
+ The silly humour makes this VN accessible even to those who are not into Japanese culture, making it excellent (and affordable) for those seeking to dip into the genre;
+ While short, the main routes are solid and varied, ranging from tear-jerkers to plain WTF, with some hilarity in between (try Okosan's route first of all!)
+ The "hidden" (and arguably "canon") route presents a very interesting darker tale;
+ The OST and visuals are not mind-blowing, but they are pleasant and do their job.
+- While I did say it was a fine VN for beginners, it is still a parody of the dating sim genre and thus some of its content might fly over your head;
+- The ending of the "hidden" route might be considered too convoluted by some, although I would say the journey is still worth it, no matter what opinion you might have of the ending.
- While the main routes being a bit on the short side isn't a big deal and not something I can complain too much about considering the game's price, I do think some routes could've been fleshed out a little more;
- The translation has some typos and English oddities.
VERDICT: If you think that this game is just a gimmick, play it and let yourself be surprised! With more than what meets the eye (you can easily clock 6-8h if you complete all routes), Hatoful Boyfriend was an excellent surprise and should be considered by all those who enjoy Visual Novels or plot-heavy games. If you are looking for gameplay-heavy elements, however, you WILL be disappointed, but that's just how VNs are.

